# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#on-the-wire
# provenance: PV-0001, PV-0002, PV-0003, PV-0004, PV-0200
# kind: ni-stream
# description: A ping frame between two other frames (as when the server pings mid-step): the framer yields it as the second of three ordinary frames.
# derivation: Each frame is a u32 BE length of its payload only (PV-0001..PV-0003); frame 2 is the framed ping of PV-0200 (literal PV-0004); frames 1 and 3 carry arbitrary opaque payloads of 8 and 3 bytes.
# expect.frames: 3
# expect.frame.1.offset: 4
# expect.frame.1.length: 8
# expect.frame.2.offset: 16
# expect.frame.2.length: 8
# expect.frame.3.offset: 28
# expect.frame.3.length: 3
# expect.error: none
# expect.trailing: 0
hex:
00 00 00 08                                       # frame 1: length 8
11 22 33 44 55 66 77 88                           # frame 1: payload (opaque)
00 00 00 08                                       # frame 2: length 8
4E 49 5F 50 49 4E 47 00                           # frame 2: N I _ P I N G \0
00 00 00 03                                       # frame 3: length 3
AA BB CC                                          # frame 3: payload (opaque)
